The check reads the patch itself (it may contain no absolute path) and then requires the milestone log to have
exactly those two rows and to have them struck through — the second half being a guard: if the rows disappear
entirely, the check has stopped looking at anything. Narrow on purpose: every other row in those tables is a
judgement, and running a text search over judgements is exactly how round 164 produced two checks that would have
