prerelease tag — so a broad-looking `>=0.0.1-rc.1 <0.2.0` silently excludes every `0.1.0-rc.*`. cordis and
schemastery are released versions, so plain ranges are correct for them; `dsh-tools` is installed as `0.1.5-rc.2`,
so its peer range is the documented explicit-branch form.

