added instead, asking a question no assertion had asked before: what happens when a project does TWO things at
once. A delivery render pins the revision it started for, and the current pointer can move underneath it — a
restore during the render must be honoured and must not be undone when the render finishes, and a patch
committed during a render must not be hijacked by it. Both directions are asserted (readings: `{restored:
true, jobRevision: r0002, pointer: r0001}` and `{jobRevision: r0001, pointer: r0002}`), and the mutation that
makes a finished delivery re-point the project at its own revision goes red.

